 "hypothesis": "daemon-side attach wall scales ~linearly with retained-window size (wire messages), and at Kevin-scale (~442k ctx) windows the attach phase is a growing, parity-safe target: at tip 60e2e198c the attach pays a full retained-window fold for the summary scalars (session_summary -> SessionFile::messages clone) plus a second fold for the snapshot payload, on top of the wire encode; the supervisor-routed fallback additionally parses + re-encodes the whole response.",
 "approach": "BASELINE ONLY (no product edit). Pure tip release binary (rustc 1.98.1) on one 16c/32GB VM, same-VM sequential fresh-daemon probes over the REAL wire (supervisor socket + direct worker transport via ticket+peer_auth), 3 creates x per-fixture: create wall, noop floor (get_session_header), get_state (summary-fold proxy), get_messages (payload fold+encode proxy), slim attaches (supervisor-routed = CLI/fallback path; the supervisor forces slim for every socket client), direct-transport attaches (the pa-tui primary path: fresh link = open-like, reused link = Esc round-trip-like), direct get_state/get_messages (relay-free proxies), daemon worker RSS/PSS + per-command worker CPU deltas, wire bytes + message counts, one raw wire dump per fixture+kind, per-trial fixture prehash asserted (source pristine; post-copy grows by bookkeeping rows), pre/mid/post CPU calibration + loadavg gates.",
