  "interpretation": "Attach wall scales ~linearly with retained wire size on BOTH client paths (direct 13.3->17.5->48.3->79.4ms across 1.45/1.66/4.29/9.48MB wire). The pa-tui primary (direct-transport) attach at the ~454k-ctx-equiv proxy is ~48ms, ~31% of it the summary fold (get_state relay-free 14.9ms) and ~69% the payload fold+encode+write (direct_msgs 36.7ms incl. one extra deep clone vs attach). The supervisor-routed fallback (and every non-direct client) pays an additional ~36-54ms parse+re-encode relay at scale. The 316k real fixture's wire is dominated by message/custom_message rows (custom thread_goal_state rows are skipped by SessionFile::messages), so wire-message count - not raw retained bytes - is the honest scaling variable."
 },
